    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Create a final UX research synthesis for the following project.\n\nPROJECT CONTEXT\n\nProject ID:\n{{ $json.project_id }}\n\nProject name:\n{{ $json.project_name }}\n\nResearch goal:\n{{ $json.research_goal }}\n\nProduct description:\n{{ $json.product_description }}\n\nRequested by:\n{{ $json.requested_by }}\n\nINTERVIEW FINDINGS\n\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.interview_findings, null, 2) }}\n\nCOMPETITIVE SYNTHESIS\n\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.competitive_synthesis, null, 2) }}\n\nTASK\n\n1. Copy project_id exactly from PROJECT CONTEXT.\n2. Copy research_goal exactly from PROJECT CONTEXT.\n3. Write an executive_summary of approximately 4 to 7 sentences that explains:\n   - what users experience,\n   - the most important problems,\n   - relevant competitive context,\n   - and the main product direction.\n\n4. Identify the most important key_findings.\n   Each key finding must contain:\n   - finding\n   - evidence_source\n   - supporting_evidence\n   - priority\n\n5. evidence_source must be one of:\n   - interview\n   - competitive\n   - combined\n\n6. priority must be one of:\n   - high\n   - medium\n   - low\n\n7. Identify evidence-based user_needs.\n   User needs must primarily come from interview findings.\n\n8. Create jobs_to_be_done only when the evidence supports them.\n   Use this structure:\n   - situation\n   - motivation\n   - expected_outcome\n\n9. Identify product_opportunities by combining user evidence with relevant competitive evidence.\n   Each opportunity must contain:\n   - opportunity\n   - rationale\n   - evidence_source\n   - priority\n\n10. Create a short roadmap:\n    - now\n    - next\n    - later\n\n11. Provide concise design_recommendations that a product design team could act on.\n\n12. List research_limitations, including limitations caused by:\n    - small interview sample size,\n    - incomplete evidence,\n    - inconsistent or low-confidence competitive sources.\n\n13. Set confidence between 0 and 1.\n\nIMPORTANT\n\n- Do not invent personas.\n- Do not invent quantitative claims.\n- Do not claim that a pattern is common across users when it appears in only one interview.\n- Do not convert general competitive advice into confirmed user needs.\n- If jobs-to-be-done are not adequately supported, return an empty array.\n- Return only the structured result required by the output parser.\n\nCall the formatter tool exactly once.\n\nPass the complete result inside its single required argument named \"output\".\n\nDo not add another wrapper such as result, response, synthesis, or research_synthesis.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a Senior UX Research Synthesis Analyst.\n\nYour task is to combine evidence from user interview findings and competitive UX research into one concise, decision-ready product research synthesis.\n\nUse only the project context, interview findings, and competitive synthesis supplied in the user message.\n\nGROUNDING RULES\n\n- Never use outside knowledge.\n- Never invent user needs, pain points, behaviors, competitor features, market gaps, or product opportunities.\n- Every conclusion must be supported by the supplied interview findings, competitive synthesis, or both.\n- Give interview evidence priority when describing user pain points and needs.\n- Use competitive evidence to provide context, identify patterns, and support product opportunities.\n- Clearly distinguish direct user evidence from competitive research evidence.\n- Do not treat missing evidence as a negative finding.\n- Avoid duplicate or overlapping findings.\n- Keep the synthesis concise, specific, and useful for product design decisions.\n- If evidence is insufficient for a field, return an empty array or state the limitation clearly.\n- Confidence must reflect the quantity, quality, and consistency of the supplied evidence.\n\nOUTPUT RULES\n\n- Copy project_id and research_goal exactly from the supplied project context.\n- Use only the fields required by the connected output parser.\n- Never add, remove, or rename output fields.\n- Return only the required structured result.\n\nFORMATTER TOOL RULE\n\nWhen calling the formatter tool, pass exactly one top-level argument named \"output\".\n\nPlace the complete structured result inside that \"output\" argument.\n\nDo not pass synthesis fields directly as top-level tool arguments."
        }
      },
